# Naming conventions

This is the naming contract of the workspace. AI agents must derive every
artifact name from the entity name using the tables below — never invent a new
style. The examples use a `Product` entity; substitute your entity name and
apply the same transformations.

## Transformations

Given the entity name `Product`:

- **PascalCase** — `Product` — Java classes, Angular classes, TypeScript types
- **camelCase** — `product` — variables, Angular model file names
- **kebab-case plural** — `products` — routes, REST paths, Angular folders
- **snake_case plural** — `products` — table and column names

## Backend artifacts (entity `Product`)

| Artifact | Path | Name rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Entity | `domain/Product.java` | `<Entity>` |
| Service | `service/ProductService.java` | `<Entity>Service` |
| Repository | `repository/ProductRepository.java` | `<Entity>Repository` |
| Controller | `controller/ProductController.java` | `<Entity>Controller` |
| Request DTO | `web/dto/ProductRequest.java` | `<Entity>Request` |
| Response DTO | `web/dto/ProductResponse.java` | `<Entity>Response` |
| Mapper | `web/mapper/ProductMapper.java` | `<Entity>Mapper` |
| Not-found exception | `exception/ProductNotFoundException.java` | `<Entity>NotFoundException` |
| Create migration | `db/migration/V2__create_products_table.sql` | `V<n>__create_<table>_table` |
| Update migration | `db/migration/V3__update_products_<change>.sql` | `V<n>__update_<table>_<change>` |
| Seed migration | `db/migration/V4__seed_products.sql` | `V<n>__seed_<table>` |

## Frontend artifacts (entity `Product`)

{{#if project.options.frontend}}
| Artifact | Path | Name rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Model | `src/app/models/product.ts` | `<entity>.ts`, exports `interface Product` and `ProductInput` |
| Service | `src/app/services/product.service.ts` | `<entity>.service.ts`, exports `class ProductService` |
| List page | `src/app/pages/products/list/list.component.ts` | selector `app-products-list` |
| Detail page | `src/app/pages/products/detail/detail.component.ts` | selector `app-products-detail` |
| Form page | `src/app/pages/products/form/form.component.ts` | selector `app-products-form` |
| Routes | `products`, `products/new`, `products/:id`, `products/:id/edit` | kebab-case plural |
| REST base | `/api/products` | kebab-case plural behind `/api` |
{{else}}
This workspace was generated without a frontend.
{{/if}}

## General rules

1. Java packages are lowercase single words: `domain`, `service`, `repository`,
   `controller`, `dto`, `mapper`, `config`, `security`, `exception`.
2. Java methods and fields are camelCase; constants are UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
3. Angular file names are kebab-case with Angular suffixes:
   `product.service.ts`, `list.component.ts`.
4. TypeScript types are PascalCase, members camelCase; model files export the
   API interface plus a matching `<Entity>Input` payload type.
5. Database names are snake_case; tables are plural, columns singular.
6. REST paths are kebab-case plural nouns under `/api`; actions that do not fit
   CRUD use sub-resources, for example `/api/orders/{id}/cancel`.
7. Tests mirror the tested file: `ProductServiceTest` next to the Java class,
   `<name>.component.spec.ts` next to the Angular component.
8. Descriptors are PascalCase singular YAML files in `entities/`:
   `entities/Product.yaml`.

When none of the tables above cover a new artifact, choose the closest rule and
document the addition inside the protected region below so the next agent
follows the same convention.

